  {
    "id": "com-ktechpit-ultimate-media-downloader",
    "name": "Ultimate Media Downloader",
    "aliases": [],
    "summary": "Media Downloader for YouTube and 1500+ other websites",
    "description": "\n      Ultimate Media Downloader is a fast and open source YouTube downloader for\n      Linux and a video downloader for more than 1500 other websites. It saves\n      videos, playlists, channels, live streams and music from YouTube,\n      Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X (Twitter), Reddit, Vimeo, SoundCloud,\n      Twitch, Kick, Dailymotion, Rumble, Odysee, Bilibili, Bandcamp, Mixcloud,\n      Pinterest, Tumblr, Streamable and the Internet Archive. Copy a link from\n      Chrome, Firefox or any browser, paste it, pick a preset and download.\n    \n      Why choose Ultimate Media Downloader?\n      \n        YouTube video downloader: save videos as MP4, MKV or WEBM in any quality from 144p and 720p HD to 1080p Full HD, 4K and 8K, including 60 fps\n        YouTube to MP3 converter, MP3 downloader and music downloader: download YouTube Music songs, albums and playlists, and extract audio as MP3 at 128 to 320 kbps, M4A, Opus or lossless FLAC with tags and cover art\n        YouTube playlist downloader and channel downloader: list an entire playlist or channel in seconds and pick exactly the items you want\n        YouTube Shorts, live streams and premieres: download Shorts, record a live stream while it runs and grab the VOD afterwards\n        Batch downloader and download manager: queue many links, download them all at once, watch progress and open finished files from the download library\n        Subtitles and closed captions: download or embed subtitles in the languages a video offers, including auto-generated captions, as SRT, VTT or ASS\n        Sign-in required, private, members-only and age-restricted videos: log in once with your Google account in the built-in Chromium-based browser and download what your account can watch\n        YouTube search built in: find videos and playlists inside the app and play them without ads\n        Custom format selector: choose the exact resolution, codec, container and bitrate when a preset is not enough\n        Dark theme, drag and drop, clipboard link detection and a download engine that updates itself so website changes are handled quickly\n      \n      More than a YouTube downloader\n      \n        Social video downloader: Facebook video downloader, Instagram Reels and video downloader, TikTok downloader, X (Twitter) video downloader, Reddit video downloader with audio, Pinterest and Tumblr\n        Streaming and live: Twitch VOD and clip downloader, Kick, Dailymotion, Rumble, Odysee, Bilibili, Streamable and live stream recording\n        Music and podcasts: SoundCloud downloader, Bandcamp, Mixcloud and podcast downloader, saved as MP3, M4A, Opus or FLAC\n        Any page with a video: HLS (m3u8) and DASH streams, direct MP4 and MP3 links, embedded players on news sites, blogs, forums and the Internet Archive\n      \n      \n      Built on yt-dlp. Ultimate Media Downloader is a graphical yt-dlp GUI and a\n      friendly front end for the youtube-dl successor: every site, format and\n      option yt-dlp supports is available from the interface, with no command\n      line and no terminal. The yt-dlp engine updates itself inside the app, so\n      a YouTube or TikTok change is fixed in hours, not at the next release.\n    \n      \n      Works with the browser you already use. Copy a video link from Google\n      Chrome, Chromium, Firefox, Brave or Edge and the app picks it up from the\n      clipboard. The built-in Chromium-based browser lets you sign in to\n      YouTube, Google, Twitch or Instagram once, so private, unlisted,\n      subscriber-only and age-restricted videos download like any other link.\n    \n      \n      Free, open source and offline: nothing is uploaded to a server, there are\n      no ads, no watermarks added and no daily limits. A native YouTube desktop\n      app, video downloader app and 4K video downloader for any Linux desktop\n      (Ubuntu, Fedora, Debian, Arch, openSUSE and Steam Deck via Flatpak), and a\n      free alternative to 4KTUBE, 4K Video Downloader, SnapTube, online video\n      downloaders and YouTube to MP3 converter websites.\n    \n    ",
    "homepage": null,
    "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
    "developer": "Keshav Bhatt",
    "binaries": [],
    "latest": null,
    "platforms": [
